HST Office: HST Sheets formulas follow the leading spreadsheet application's conventions in every
language and locale (owner request 2026-11-13: users coming from it must not stumble).

- i18npool vi_VN.xml: the locale's boolean words are "true"/"false" (upstream "đúng"/"sai"), so
  booleans show TRUE/FALSE in a Vietnamese-locale document, typing TRUE/FALSE in a cell gives a
  boolean, and =TRUE in a formula works. Files are unaffected: ODF and .xlsx store booleans as
  values, never as these words.
- sc compiler.cxx: TRUE and FALSE written without parentheses are the boolean constants whatever
  the document locale (before, a vi-VN document turned =FALSE, VLOOKUP(...;FALSE) and
  AND(TRUE;...) into #NAME?), and a boolean constant gives a boolean result like TRUE().
- formula FormulaCompiler.cxx: the UI (native grammar) prints TRUE()/FALSE() without arguments as
  TRUE/FALSE, so a typed =TRUE reads =TRUE in the input line; ODFF and OOXML keep TRUE()/FALSE().
- sc global.cxx: cells show the leading application's error values only (#VALUE!, #NUM!, #NAME?,
  #REF!, #DIV/0!, #N/A, #NULL!, #SPILL!); "Err:5xx" (Vietnamese "Lỗi:5xx"), #ADDIN? and #MACRO?
  are gone. The cause stays in the status bar. Same mapping as the .xlsx export.
- officecfg Calc.xcs: the default formula syntax is Excel A1 (Sheet1!A1, 'Trang tính1'!A1)
  instead of Calc A1 ($Sheet1.A1). the Formula options page still switches it, an
  explicit profile value wins. ODF files keep storing OpenFormula ([.A1]) whatever the UI syntax.
- formula core_resource.hrc, sc scfuncs.hrc, vi sc/messages.po: CEILING and FLOOR typed in the UI
  are the functions of that name in .xlsx files (upstream named them CEILING.XCL/FLOOR.XCL and
  gave CEILING/FLOOR the OpenDocument rounding, saved to .xlsx as CEILING.MATH/FLOOR.MATH); the
  OpenDocument variants are shown as CEILING.ODF/FLOOR.ODF. Only the UI names change (native and
  English-function-name lists): ODF, .xlsx and the macro API keep their names. Their help text no
  longer calls them a compatibility function of an old product version. Likewise FORMULATEXT, SKEW.P,
  FORECAST.ETS, FORECAST.ETS.CONFINT and FORECAST.ETS.STAT are the UI names of the functions upstream
  shows as FORMULA, SKEWP, FORECAST.ETS.ADD, FORECAST.ETS.PI.ADD and FORECAST.ETS.STAT.ADD (their
  .xlsx names; ODF keeps FORMULA, SKEWP, ...).

- sc xetable.cxx: a formula kept with a syntax error (LibreOffice accepts "=1+*2" and shows an error)
  is not written to .xlsx, only its error result: the leading application refused the whole file
  (also with repair), measured with Office 2021 on 2026-11-13.

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: tests/unit/test_sheets_excel_formula_conventions.py,
tests/runtime/check-sheets-excel-formula-conventions.py.
